# DURABLE REPRO — the "zero-cost move" suggestion advises code the compiler
# REJECTS. Not occasionally: in 100% of cases it can fire.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD). Build this program and the compiler says:
#     warning: argument `v` is last use — pass as `!v` for zero-cost move
# Take exactly that advice — change `passthru(v)` to `passthru(!v)` — and the
# compiler rejects it at the SAME span:
#     error[E_OwnershipMismatch]: ownership mismatch for `a`: the parameter only
#     borrows — it does not consume the argument;
#     help: remove the `!` (the value is not moved into this call)
#
# So the compiler tells the user to write `!v`, then tells them to remove it.
#
# ⚠ WHY IT IS 100%, not a corner case — single-writer chain, verified:
#   * `move_suggestions` is pushed at exactly one site (`exprs/calls.rs:1574`),
#     gated on `fn_consumed_params`;
#   * `fn_consumed_params` is written at exactly one site
#     (`context.rs:1196`), inside `record_param_cloned`;
#   * `record_param_cloned` early-returns unless `is_bare_param`
#     (`context.rs:1192`).
# So EVERY move suggestion the compiler can emit names a BARE param — and under
# ratified D31 full-strict, `!` at a bare-param call site is always
# `E_OwnershipMismatch`. There is no input for which this advice is valid.
#
# ⚠ The warning fires on `gg build` but NOT on `gg check`, so a `gg check`-based
# assertion is a FALSE NEGATIVE for this defect. The wired test builds.
#
# ⚠ NOT introduced by any in-flight track — this ships at HEAD. It reaches the
# user through `record_param_cloned`'s SECOND caller (`stmts/mod.rs:1892`, the
# throws-Ptr leg of `lower_return`), which is why the throws shape below is
# load-bearing and must not be "simplified" away.
#
# INTENDED: no "zero-cost move" warning here — the callee only borrows, so
# there is no move to suggest. (The alternative reading, making `!` legal at
# this position, is REJECTED: D31 full-strict ratified that `!` spells
# contractual consumption, and this parameter does not consume.)
#
# The wired test asserts the INTENDED state: `gg build` succeeds and its stderr
# does NOT contain "zero-cost move".

Vector[int] passthru(Vector[int] a) throws String:
    return a

void main():
    Vector[int] v = [9, 8, 7]
    Vector[int] w = passthru(v)! catch (m): [0]
    print(w.len())
